{"id":"8fc074624288fbbb","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-brownian.md","title":"Brownian Motion","display":"df-brownian — Brownian Motion","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-brownian","aliases":["58-df-brownian"],"display":"df-brownian — Brownian Motion","depends_on":["[[58-df-stochastic-process]]","[[58-df-gaussian]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-brownian"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-brownian</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-brownian — Brownian Motion"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" href=\"?note=b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" title=\"58-df-stochastic-process\">58-df-stochastic-process</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c96eb70b5fd08810\" href=\"?note=c96eb70b5fd08810\" title=\"58-df-gaussian\">58-df-gaussian</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\((\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (probability space)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B:\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\to\\mathbb R^\\Omega\">\\(B:\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\to\\mathbb R^\\Omega\\)</span> (real-valued process)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\">\\(\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\)</span> (Borel sigma-algebra)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (nondegenerate Gaussian predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c96eb70b5fd08810\" href=\"?note=c96eb70b5fd08810\" title=\"58-df-gaussian\">58-df-gaussian</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StochProc}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{StochProc}_S\\)</span> (stochastic-process predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" href=\"?note=b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" title=\"58-df-stochastic-process\">58-df-stochastic-process</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (independent-increments predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(b,T)\">\\(\\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(b,T)\\)</span> (real-valued continuous-path predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Brownian}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Brownian}_S\\)</span> (Brownian-motion predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega)\">\\(t\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega)\\)</span> 缩写 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{\\langle t,B(t)(\\omega)\\rangle:t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\">\\(\\{\\langle t,B(t)(\\omega)\\rangle:t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\\)</span>，其他箭头函数同样为所示定义域上的函数图。连续样本路径事件需属于 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal F\">\\(\\mathcal F\\)</span>，该条件已写入正文。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brownian\\text{-}independent\\text{-}increments}\\vdash \\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(B,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land \\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\forall (t_i)_{i\\leq n}\\in(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})^{n+1}\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall i&lt;n\\;(t_i&lt;t_{i+1})\\right]\\to\\forall(A_i)_{i&lt;n}\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)^n\\;\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\bigcap_{i&lt;n}\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:B(t_{i+1})(\\omega)-B(t_i)(\\omega)\\in A_i\\}\\right)=\\prod_{i&lt;n}\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:B(t_{i+1})(\\omega)-B(t_i)(\\omega)\\in A_i\\}\\right)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brownian\\text{-}independent\\text{-}increments}\\vdash \\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(B,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land \\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\forall (t_i)_{i\\leq n}\\in(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})^{n+1}\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall i&lt;n\\;(t_i&lt;t_{i+1})\\right]\\to\\forall(A_i)_{i&lt;n}\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)^n\\;\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\bigcap_{i&lt;n}\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:B(t_{i+1})(\\omega)-B(t_i)(\\omega)\\in A_i\\}\\right)=\\prod_{i&lt;n}\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:B(t_{i+1})(\\omega)-B(t_i)(\\omega)\\in A_i\\}\\right)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brownian\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}path}\\vdash \\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(b,T)\\leftrightarrow T\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land b\\in\\mathbb R^T\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall u\\in T\\;\\left(|u-t|&lt;\\delta\\to|b(u)-b(t)|&lt;\\varepsilon\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brownian\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}path}\\vdash \\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(b,T)\\leftrightarrow T\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\land b\\in\\mathbb R^T\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall u\\in T\\;\\left(|u-t|&lt;\\delta\\to|b(u)-b(t)|&lt;\\varepsilon\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brownian} \\vdash \\mathrm{Brownian}_S(B,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(B,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land \\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:B(0)(\\omega)=0\\})=1\\land \\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\forall s,t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\left(s&lt;t\\to\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(\\omega\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega)-B(s)(\\omega);0,t-s;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\right)\\land \\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:\\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(t\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega),\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\land\\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:\\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(t\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega),\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\})=1\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brownian} \\vdash \\mathrm{Brownian}_S(B,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(B,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land \\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:B(0)(\\omega)=0\\})=1\\land \\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\forall s,t\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\left(s&lt;t\\to\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(\\omega\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega)-B(s)(\\omega);0,t-s;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\right)\\land \\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:\\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(t\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega),\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\land\\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:\\mathrm{ContinuousPath}_S(t\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega),\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\})=1\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The stochastic-process conjunct supplies the measurable random-variable typing omitted by the earlier formula.</li>\n<li>The increment passed to the Gaussian predicate is the explicit pointwise random variable <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega)-B(s)(\\omega)\">\\(\\omega\\mapsto B(t)(\\omega)-B(s)(\\omega)\\)</span>, rather than an unsourced subtraction operation on function graphs.</li>\n<li>The remaining clauses state almost-sure start at zero, independent stationary Gaussian increments, and almost-sure path continuity.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-stochastic-process","status":"resolved","id":"b5f77bed7dfe3f07","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-stochastic-process]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-gaussian","status":"resolved","id":"c96eb70b5fd08810","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-gaussian]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-gaussian","status":"resolved","id":"c96eb70b5fd08810","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ (nondegenerate Gaussian predicate, see [[58-df-gaussian]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-stochastic-process","status":"resolved","id":"b5f77bed7dfe3f07","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{StochProc}_S$ (stochastic-process predicate, see [[58-df-stochastic-process]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"B:\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\to\\mathbb R^\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{StochProc}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{IndependentIncrements}_S(B;\\O